---@field type string
---@field id string The unique ID of the memory (`mem_...`). It stays the same when the memory's path changes. To retrieve, update, or delete the memory, pass this ID.
---@field memory_store_id string ID of the memory store this memory belongs to (a `memstore_...` value).
---@field path string Hierarchical path of the memory within the store, e.g. `/projects/foo/notes.md`. Always starts with `/`. Paths are case-sensitive and unique within a store. Maximum 1,024 bytes.
---@field content? string|distilled.Null The memory's UTF-8 text content, or `null` when the response uses `view=basic`. The maximum size is 100 kB (102,400 bytes).
---@field content_size_bytes number The size of the memory's `content` in UTF-8 bytes. It is set regardless of `view`.
---@field content_sha256 string Lowercase hex SHA-256 digest of the UTF-8 `content` bytes (64 characters). The server applies no normalization, so clients can compute the same hash locally for staleness checks and as the value for a `content_sha256` precondition on update. Always populated, regardless of `view`.
---@field memory_version_id string The ID of the memory version that holds the memory's current content (`memver_...`). Memory versions don't have a flag that marks the latest one. Compare their IDs with this field instead. See the [memory guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/memory#audit-memory-changes) to learn more about memory versions.
---@field created_at string When this memory was created, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field updated_at string When the memory was last changed, in RFC 3339. To find out who made the change, look at `created_by` on the memory version that `memory_version_id` references.

