---@field type string
---@field id string The unique ID of the memory store (`memstore_...`). Use it to attach the store to a session.
---@field name string Human-readable name for the store. 1–255 characters. The store's mount-path slug under `/mnt/memory/` is derived from this name.
---@field description string Free-text description of what the store contains, up to 1,024 characters. Included in the agent's system prompt when the store is attached, so word it to be useful to the agent. Empty string when unset.
---@field created_at string When the memory store was created, in RFC 3339.
---@field updated_at string When the memory store was last changed, in RFC 3339. Changing its `name`, `description`, or `metadata` updates it. Archiving the store does too. Changes to the store's memories don't.
---@field metadata anthropic.beta_memory_stores.BetaManagedAgentsMemoryStoreMetadataMap Key-value pairs for your own use, such as the end user that the store belongs to. A store has at most 16 pairs. Keys are 1 to 64 characters long and values at most 512 characters. You can't filter lists by metadata.
---@field archived_at string|distilled.Null When the memory store was archived, in RFC 3339, or `null` if it hasn't been. Archiving can't be undone. An archived store can't be attached to new sessions. You can't create or update its memories or update the store. You can still read and delete its memories, redact their versions, and delete the store. See the [memory guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/memory#archive-a-store) to learn more about archiving.

