---@class anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryRequest
---@field memory_store_id string The ID of the memory store that holds the memory (`memstore_...`).
---@field memory_id string The ID of the memory to update (`mem_...`).
---@field view? anthropic.beta_memory_stores.BetaManagedAgentsMemoryView|string
---@field anthropicVersion? string The version of the Claude API you want to use. Read more about versioning and our version history [here](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/versioning).
---@field anthropicBeta? anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryRequestAnthropicBetaList This endpoint is in beta: requests must send `agent-memory-2026-07-22` or `managed-agents-2026-04-01` in this header.
---@field anthropicWorkspaceId? string Optional header to select the Workspace for this request. The value is a Workspace ID (for example, `wrkspc_011CZkZaBF1tNoB5wlCeusgy`). Only needed for credentials that can act on more than one Workspace. A credential that belongs to a specific Workspace may omit it; if sent, it must match that Workspace.
---@field content? string|distilled.Null New UTF-8 text content for the memory. Maximum 100 kB (102,400 bytes). Omit to leave the content unchanged (e.g., for a rename-only update).
---@field path? string|distilled.Null The new path of the memory, which renames it. Omit it to keep the current path. The memory keeps its `id`. A path starts with `/` and has 1 to 20 segments. A segment can't be empty and can't be `.` or `..`. A path can't contain control characters, format characters, or the line and paragraph separators U+2028 and U+2029. It must be in Unicode Normalization Form C and at most 1,024 bytes long. Paths are case-sensitive.
---@field precondition? anthropic.beta_memory_stores.BetaManagedAgentsContentSha256Precondition The condition that the memory must meet for the update to apply. Omit it to update unconditionally. If the condition fails, the request fails with HTTP status 409.

---This endpoint is in beta: requests must send `agent-memory-2026-07-22` or `managed-agents-2026-04-01` in this header.
---@alias anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryRequestAnthropicBetaList anthropic.beta_memory_stores.AnthropicBeta[]

---@class anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryStoreRequest
---@field memory_store_id string The ID of the memory store to update (`memstore_...`). The request fails with HTTP status 400 if the store is archived.
---@field anthropicVersion? string The version of the Claude API you want to use. Read more about versioning and our version history [here](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/versioning).
---@field anthropicBeta? anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryStoreRequestAnthropicBetaList This endpoint is in beta: requests must send `agent-memory-2026-07-22` or `managed-agents-2026-04-01` in this header.
---@field anthropicWorkspaceId? string Optional header to select the Workspace for this request. The value is a Workspace ID (for example, `wrkspc_011CZkZaBF1tNoB5wlCeusgy`). Only needed for credentials that can act on more than one Workspace. A credential that belongs to a specific Workspace may omit it; if sent, it must match that Workspace.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null The new name of the memory store, 1 to 255 characters long, without control characters. Sessions created after the change use the new name for the store's directory under `/mnt/memory/`.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null New description for the store, up to 1,024 characters. Pass an empty string to clear it.
---@field metadata? anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryStoreRequestMetadataMap|distilled.Null Changes to apply to the memory store's metadata. Keys you leave out keep their values. Set a key to a string to add or replace it, or to `null` to remove it. After the change, the metadata can hold at most 16 key-value pairs. Keys are 1 to 64 characters long and values at most 512 characters.

---This endpoint is in beta: requests must send `agent-memory-2026-07-22` or `managed-agents-2026-04-01` in this header.
---@alias anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryStoreRequestAnthropicBetaList anthropic.beta_memory_stores.AnthropicBeta[]

---@alias anthropic.beta_memory_stores.UpdateMemoryStoreRequestMetadataMap { [string]: string|distilled.Null }

